UFC 324 event marked the introduction of the promotion's updated bonus structure, which added a additional $25,000 bonuses award for finishing a fight by knockouts or submissions except for people who missed weight. 
We are trying add fighters who rightfully earned these new "Finishing Bonuses" awards in right section of UFC Event page>Bonus award section but someone might be guarding or lawyering it. 

In this source 
"Starting with UFC 324, UFC fighters who earn finishes will each pick up a $25,000 finishing bonus, though those earning Performance and Fight of the Night awards will not double up. That means Nikita Krylov and Waldo Cortes-Acosta will earn 25K extra. Alex Perez, who stopped Charles Johnson, does not qualify, as he missed weight for the bout.
"
It pretty clear they listed it and we using same MMA UFC Bonus award format that already been setup by MMA community to add that.
